# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Liferay workspace lives inside this repo, but almost none of it is source.
# What matters here is client-extensions/ — that is the code an `rm -rf` of the
# workspace once destroyed, and the reason this repo exists.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The downloaded DXP bundle: ~3 GB, reproducible with `blade gw initBundle`.
liferay-workspace/bundles/

# Build output and dependency caches, at any depth.
node_modules/
node_modules_cache/
build/
dist/
.gradle/

# Local runtime noise.
*.log
.DS_Store

# Local environment: contains an OAuth2 client id that is regenerated on every
# deploy anyway, so it is never worth committing. Rebuild it with local-env.sh.
.env

# Python bytecode from the seeder/reset scripts.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The talk's own material — the deck, its script and notes, the CFP and early
# planning — stays on the presenter's machine. This repo is the code it shows.
*.pptx
*.potx
*.ppt
*.pdf
deck/
deck.html
CFP-submission.md
OVERNIGHT-PLAN.md
TALK-OUTLINE.md
TALK-SCRIPT.md
idea-object-dashboards.md
FOLLOW-UPS.md
outfitter/record.py
outfitter/shoot.py

# The Liferay workspace template's AI-assistant rule files: generic guidance,
# not about this project, and at odds with RUNBOOK.md (blade gw deploy, the
# default password). Kept locally, not published.
liferay-workspace/.claude/
liferay-workspace/.cursor/
liferay-workspace/.gemini/
liferay-workspace/.github/
liferay-workspace/.windsurf/
liferay-workspace/.workspace-rules/
